# Every real page (home, categories, places, events, map, privacy, contacts)
# is a prerendered static file, so it's served directly — none of these rules
# ever apply to a real URL.
#
# /favorites and /admin are genuine client-only routes with no static file of
# their own (favorites is personal, admin is noindex and code-split out of
# public builds), so they still need to load the SPA shell.
/favorites       /index.html   200
/ru/favorites    /index.html   200
/ro/favorites    /index.html   200
/admin           /index.html   200
/ru/admin        /index.html   200
/ro/admin        /index.html   200

# Anything else has no matching page: a real 404, not a 200 with the home
# page's content (a "soft 404" — confuses search engines about which URLs are
# real). The SPA still mounts and shows its own not-found message.
/*    /404.html   404
